# Wave W17-P (Route 118): ford post — a ford-end post flanking the plank crossing: a sturdy post banded with white depth marks, the river’s own gauge cut for travellers — read the bands before you trust the planks (design: the ford planks are older than the road and prouder; their ends are gauged like everything the river touches in this country). On ford turf (fully opaque, ground baked in) — split from Route 119’s gauge boxes by form: this is the river’s hand-cut post gauge, that is the Institute’s instrument box.
